label CertificateTake
There is a museum display stand in the center of the room in front of me
On the stand is my sister's certificate, stating that she received the Peace Prize.
...
[signal arg="Bedroom_cerfiticateTake"]
I take the certificate from the stand into my inventory.
[end_timeline]
label CertificateUse
This is my sister’s Peace Prize certificate.
Neatly framed, flawless, and heavy with accomplishments I could only dream of.
No matter what I ever build or achieve, it will always be eclipsed by her shadow.
It’s hard not to feel small when your sibling is officially recognized as a savior of humanity.
[end_timeline]
label DrawingTake
There are photos of me and my daughters on the table.
I open the drawer and see an old drawing by Ann.
[background scene="res://scenes/dialogues/DialogicBackgroundScene.tscn" arg="res://assets/cgs/CG_Puzzle4_Drawing.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
[wait_input]
I take the drawing into my inventory.
[end_timeline]
label DrawingUse
[background scene="res://scenes/dialogues/DialogicBackgroundScene.tscn" arg="res://assets/cgs/CG_Puzzle4_Drawing.png" fade="1.0" wait="true"]
A drawing I made when I was a kid.
It’s honestly embarrassing to look at.
Mom kept it, but it’s a painful reminder that nothing I do will ever measure up to my sister.
No matter how much sentiment I pump into this piece of paper, it could never [b]weigh as much as her[/b] success.
[wait_input]
[end_timeline]